From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] cmd: blkmap: parse the linear map start block as hex

Like the other block numbers of the command and as the documented
example expects. The start block from 'part start' is hex.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 cmd/blkmap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmd/blkmap.c b/cmd/blkmap.c
index 65edec89..d5e5002d 100644
--- a/cmd/blkmap.c
+++ b/cmd/blkmap.c
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ static int do_blkmap_map_linear(struct map_ctx *ctx, int argc,
 		return CMD_RET_USAGE;
 
 	ldevnum = dectoul(argv[2], NULL);
-	lblknr = dectoul(argv[3], NULL);
+	lblknr = hextoul(argv[3], NULL);
 
 	lbd = blk_get_devnum_by_uclass_idname(argv[1], ldevnum);
 	if (!lbd) {
